        "key": "revenue-d240-monthly-audit-digest-v1",
        "destination": "fixture:owner",
        "body": "Monthly revenue digest \u2014 fixture day 240 (2027-09-01).\n\nThe later source audit changes the active compact-offer experiment's commercial conclusion. measurement-9, using settled-order-ledger-v3 with mature cancellations, corrects earlier receipts 1/4/6/7 for the same original sessions. Revenue is $5.00/session for detailed versus $4.80 for compact: -$0.20 (-4%), reported 95% difference interval [-$0.30,-$0.10], 10,000 sessions per arm, exposure verified and mature. This supersedes the earlier +7% estimate; it is not a new independent cohort. Mature refund rates are 2% in each arm and checkout errors 0.2% in each arm. Separate guardrail denominators/uncertainty and raw ledger/assignment rows remain unavailable.\n\nI rolled back the currently active experiment under the standing revenue authorization. Settlement effect-10 and independent status confirm revision 3 now serves detailed with wallet_tracking=true, the experiment is closed, and four related evaluations remain active. Compatible footer work is unaffected. This is separate from historical Spruce-47 and its already-completed rb-733 rollback.\n\nPost-restoration measurement-11 repeats the same original-session audit and corrects measurement-9. Neither it nor elapsed fixture time establishes post-rollback recovery. No recovery benefit is claimed. No billed validations were used; the shared whole-product ledger remains 9 of 10 credits consumed with no automatic reset.\n\nThe revenue responsibility remains active. Schedule effect-12 confirms a future run on fixture day 254 (2027-09-15), 14 days after restoration, to check new post-restoration exposure/outcomes, audits and revenue opportunities. Fresh windows and adequate evidence will be required; repeated corrected observations will not be pooled. No owner decision is needed. Evidence and correction chain are retained in memory/evidence/day-240-*.json and memory/day-240-session-record.md."
      },
